---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="The browser technologies used by this website, and how you can control them."
>
  <section>
    <h2>What cookies are</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small pieces of information a website can store in your browser. Some are
      temporary; others remain until they expire or you delete them. Browser storage and tracking
      scripts are related technologies, but traffic statistics do not necessarily require cookies.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Our website features</h2>
    <p>
      The current website application does not set its own cookies or use local storage or session
      storage to persist visitor information. It has no advertising cookies, Google Analytics, Meta
      Pixel, embedded social feeds or third-party font loading. Fonts, images and brand logos are
      hosted with the website.
    </p>
    <p>
      The contact form sends your details only when you submit it. It does not use a browser cookie
      to remember your inquiry. Email delivery through Brevo happens on the server; the form does
      not load a Brevo advertising or tracking widget in your browser.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Cloudflare hosting, security and traffic statistics</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare hosts and protects this site and provides traffic statistics from requests handled
      by its network. This involves processing technical request information and is separate from a
      browser-based advertising tracker. We did not observe a Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon in the
      page scripts when reviewing the site on October 11, 2026.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on the security features enabled and the checks needed for a particular visit,
      Cloudflare may set cookies to distinguish legitimate traffic from bots or remember a completed
      security challenge. These are used for security rather than advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      For example, <code>__cf_bm</code> may be used when Cloudflare bot protection is enabled;
      Cloudflare describes it as expiring after 30 minutes of inactivity. A{' '}
      <code>cf_clearance</code> cookie may record a passed security check, with its lifetime
      depending on the challenge configuration. These are conditional examples, not a claim that
      both cookies are set on every visit. A normal page inspection cannot rule out cookies issued
      during a later security challenge.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare explains its security cookies and their lifetimes in its{' '}
      <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/">
        cookie documentation
      </a>
      . Our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains provider processing and possible
      processing outside Canada.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Your browser controls</h2>
    <p>
      You can view, delete or block cookies in your browser’s privacy or site-data settings. The
      exact controls depend on your browser. Blocking security cookies may cause repeated checks or
      prevent a protected page from loading. Deleting browser cookies does not delete an inquiry
      already delivered by email; contact us to discuss that information.
    </p>
    <p>
      We have not added an “Accept all” banner because the current site does not offer optional
      advertising or browser-based analytics cookies. If optional tracking is introduced, we will
      review the required choices and consent controls before enabling it, and update this policy.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
    <p>
      Facebook, Instagram and other external destinations may use their own cookies after you follow
      a link. Their policies and controls apply on those websites.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Questions and changes</h2>
    <p>
      Contact Gavyn Robinson using the details below with questions about this policy. We review it
      when website features or provider settings change and update the effective date accordingly.
    </p>
  </section>
</PolicyLayout>
